  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>k</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>K</mi></math> be the minimum and the maximum values of the function <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>0.6</mn></msup><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>0.6</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mi>&#160;</mi><mtext>in</mtext><mi>&#160;</mi><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>, respectively, then the ordered pair <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>)</mo></math> is equal to:",
